WEBVTT

00:04.220 --> 00:05.262
Hey, when you get a second,

00:05.304 --> 00:06.888
let me see that key
I risked my life for,

00:07.223 --> 00:08.265
Narancia.

00:08.474 --> 00:09.475
Huh?

00:09.850 --> 00:11.268
- Here.
- Wait! Don't throw it!

00:13.062 --> 00:14.563
Ouch, freakin' cazzone!

00:14.689 --> 00:16.607
What a drama queen.

00:16.691 --> 00:20.486
You've got feeling.
Isn't that a good thing?

00:20.569 --> 00:24.239
I got the damn thing reattached
thirty minutes ago, you fool…

00:24.281 --> 00:28.118
It hurts like a mother… Dammit!

00:30.121 --> 00:33.791
You safeguarded my daughter's life.
You have my gratitude, Bucciarati.

00:33.833 --> 00:35.876
Proceed to Napoli Centrale,
binario six,

00:35.918 --> 00:38.128
look for the turtle
at the water fountain,

00:38.212 --> 00:40.005
and use this key.

00:40.089 --> 00:43.634
You are to take her
to Venezia by train.

00:44.051 --> 00:48.551
P.S. My directives will cease
upon your safe arrival in Venezia.

00:48.764 --> 00:51.516
What the hell are we supposed to
find by the water fountain?

00:51.600 --> 00:53.977
The boss said there was
a way for us to travel

00:54.019 --> 00:55.770
while staying under
the radar of the enemy.

00:55.938 --> 00:58.815
It'll be risky for sure,
but we have no choice but to trust.

00:58.858 --> 01:01.610
Think the boss is already there?

01:01.694 --> 01:03.153
I mean it kinda sounds like it…

01:03.320 --> 01:05.280
Whether he is doesn't concern us.

01:05.322 --> 01:07.324
Our focus remains fulfilling
our directive.

01:07.950 --> 01:10.410
There's an espresso bound
for Firenze in ten minutes.

01:10.453 --> 01:11.537
We have to catch it.

01:11.662 --> 01:13.288
Mista, we alone?

01:13.330 --> 01:15.206
For the time being,
looks like we're in the clear.

01:15.583 --> 01:17.334
It'll be another story
at the station, though.

01:17.418 --> 01:19.545
The place will be crawling
with paid informants

01:19.628 --> 01:20.962
just itching to tip off the enemy.

01:22.506 --> 01:24.841
<i>I can't imagine what it'd be like…</i>

01:25.676 --> 01:27.678
<i>Suddenly, you've got
a target on your back,</i>

01:27.762 --> 01:29.346
<i>and all because of
a father you've never known.</i>

01:29.430 --> 01:31.515
<i>Must be terrifying…</i>

01:31.766 --> 01:33.809
Oh, I feel ya, Fugo…

01:35.019 --> 01:37.104
I've been a little
preoccupied, too,

01:37.146 --> 01:39.189
if you know what I mean…

01:39.231 --> 01:40.232
Huh?

01:44.236 --> 01:46.404
Th-That's…

01:51.994 --> 01:54.079
Please, you gotta excuse
this poor schlub!

01:54.163 --> 01:56.540
I know it looks bad,
but it's not what you're thinking!

01:56.749 --> 01:58.876
I promise he wasn't
slamming on the breaks

01:58.918 --> 02:01.086
just to sneak a peek
of your perfect tits

02:01.170 --> 02:02.880
or cope a feel of
your slamming thighs!

02:03.005 --> 02:04.548
He just couldn't help himself!

02:04.632 --> 02:05.633
Hey, shut up, okay?!

02:05.674 --> 02:06.966
I was fighting for
my life back there

02:07.009 --> 02:09.052
and you make it sound like
I was aiming for second base!

02:09.094 --> 02:13.431
Just whatever you do,
don't tell the boss!

02:24.485 --> 02:28.985
<i>Heavy stones of fate
are holding down my dreams</i>

02:29.824 --> 02:33.285
<i>It feels as if I'm being crushed</i>

02:35.037 --> 02:39.537
<i>I've been staggering around
with nowhere to hide</i>

02:40.209 --> 02:44.087
<i>But I will never give in</i>

02:44.129 --> 02:48.629
<i>I know there are fragments of hope
buried beneath all that rubble</i>

02:55.891 --> 03:00.391
<i>I will find them with my own hands
and turn this world upside down</i>

03:08.988 --> 03:13.488
<i>Fighting gold
We will shine one day</i>

03:14.952 --> 03:19.452
<i>As long as we continue to
believe in our own path</i>

03:22.042 --> 03:25.170
<i>We are unyielding souls</i>

03:25.254 --> 03:29.754
<i>Our battle against god
will keep raging on</i>

03:30.467 --> 03:34.967
<i>Until our final days
Fighting gold</i>

03:44.481 --> 03:48.359
EPISODE 14
IL TRENO ESPRESSO PER FIRENZE

03:48.944 --> 03:51.196
FLORENCE BOUND LEAVING AT
16:35 FROM PLATFORM 6

04:03.792 --> 04:06.544
He's really here.
That's Bucciarati.

04:07.296 --> 04:09.548
I don't freakin' believe it.

04:09.632 --> 04:12.176
He actually showed up to
the station in broad daylight.

04:12.217 --> 04:13.760
I'll butcher that bastard!

04:15.137 --> 04:17.848
Maybe all the pressure finally
got to the stronzo,

04:17.932 --> 04:22.432
or maybe he thinks he's figured out
a way to throw us off the trail.

04:23.771 --> 04:25.856
Who gives a shit?
I'm gonna butcher that punk!

04:26.148 --> 04:29.317
He killed Formaggio and Illuso!
I'm gonna butcher him!

04:29.360 --> 04:30.361
Hey, moron.

04:31.195 --> 04:33.488
Cool it with the butcher crap,
capisce?

04:33.530 --> 04:35.073
It's annoying as hell.

04:36.408 --> 04:39.702
We don't talk like that,
not our squadra of mafiosi.

04:40.037 --> 04:42.706
They are words for the completely
and utterly weak.

04:42.873 --> 04:45.417
'Cause by the time anything
remotely close

04:45.501 --> 04:48.253
comes to my mind
or the mind of my fellow mafiosi,

04:48.629 --> 04:52.883
our victim is already butchered.
Everything is finito, understand?!

04:53.092 --> 04:55.427
Such words have
never crossed my lips.

04:55.511 --> 04:58.472
You will follow my example,
right, Pesci?

04:58.514 --> 05:00.140
That is,
if you're really one of us.

05:00.808 --> 05:03.644
Understand what I'm sayin'?

05:05.938 --> 05:08.982
Yeah… I gotcha, big bro!

05:09.024 --> 05:11.860
I gotta say butchered,
not butcher.

05:12.611 --> 05:14.529
Prosciutto…

05:15.114 --> 05:17.658
I'll head over on
the platform here.

05:17.700 --> 05:21.537
Pesci, you get on and head to
the front car from the inside.

05:21.704 --> 05:22.705
Got it!

05:23.706 --> 05:25.082
We'll get him from both sides.

05:25.708 --> 05:28.085
We need the boss's daughter alive,
after all.

05:36.010 --> 05:39.096
Bucciarati, we're coming up
on the departure time.

05:39.179 --> 05:40.430
Is something wrong?

05:41.015 --> 05:44.101
Looks like this is the only
water fountain around here…

05:45.060 --> 05:47.729
There's no way this was designed
for this key hole.

05:48.147 --> 05:50.107
Besides…

05:50.274 --> 05:52.776
you don't even need
a key to open it.

05:52.818 --> 05:54.277
It's just an access hatch.

05:56.196 --> 05:59.199
Bucciarati, how about the lock
on that fire hydrant?

06:01.660 --> 06:03.286
It's not a match either.

06:03.370 --> 06:07.207
I can't find any lock
or door that will fit.

06:07.291 --> 06:08.667
How can this be the right place?!

06:14.381 --> 06:16.132
Should we pass on this train?

06:16.425 --> 06:17.717
The next train in fifteen minutes

06:17.760 --> 06:19.011
- is bound for Roma.
- No!

06:19.511 --> 06:22.722
They probably already know we're here and
are heading to the station as we speak.

06:22.765 --> 06:24.808
We can't stay here any longer!

06:24.933 --> 06:26.142
Binario six…

06:26.226 --> 06:27.810
The turtle by the water fountain…

06:27.936 --> 06:30.104
This has to be the spot!

06:30.147 --> 06:31.982
Damn it! What's—

06:37.029 --> 06:38.030
The turtle…

06:56.381 --> 06:59.467
Hey, Pesci, what the hell
are you doing here?

06:59.718 --> 07:01.845
I-I should be
asking you that, big bro!

07:01.887 --> 07:04.598
Where did Bucciarati go?

07:12.815 --> 07:15.901
I saw Bucciarati board
the train right before my eyes.

07:16.068 --> 07:17.694
There's no way you wouldn't
have passed him

07:17.736 --> 07:19.404
walking down the aisles
of this entire train.

07:19.530 --> 07:21.657
Well? I'm right, aren't I?

07:21.698 --> 07:24.117
I didn't see any of them!

07:24.159 --> 07:25.869
Not Bucciarati,
not his annoying friends,

07:25.953 --> 07:27.663
not that new guy, or that bitch,

07:27.704 --> 07:29.956
none of them!

07:32.000 --> 07:34.544
This doesn't sit right with me…

07:36.672 --> 07:39.174
Big bro, it's just about
bye-bye time.

07:39.341 --> 07:41.343
They've gotta be
sneaking around here

07:41.385 --> 07:42.886
somewhere in the station.

07:42.928 --> 07:44.721
They're waiting to spot us

07:44.763 --> 07:47.390
before getting on
another train to get away.

07:47.808 --> 07:49.434
- Let's grab some train station drifter
<i>- There was something</i>

07:49.518 --> 07:51.853
- and have him track em down!
<i>- by that water fountain.</i>

07:52.146 --> 07:53.522
<i>He must've picked it up.</i>

07:54.565 --> 07:59.065
<i>He grabbed something dark
by the fountain!</i>

07:59.903 --> 08:01.237
Get on, Pesci!

08:02.114 --> 08:03.907
- But why?!
- Call it a gut feeling.

08:04.074 --> 08:05.283
I don't know how,
but I have a hunch

08:05.367 --> 08:06.993
Bucciarati and his little yes men

08:07.035 --> 08:09.245
are hiding somewhere on this train.

08:09.329 --> 08:10.747
You have a hunch?

08:11.290 --> 08:12.040
A hunch!

08:12.040 --> 08:15.251
The boss must be offering them
some kind of assistance.

08:15.294 --> 08:18.255
I have a hunch that if we don't
pick over this train right now,

08:18.338 --> 08:20.715
we will lose those goons forever!

08:20.757 --> 08:21.549
A hunch?

08:21.592 --> 08:23.802
Shut your hole and
get on the train, Pesci!

08:26.054 --> 08:28.848
<i>A three and a half hour
train journey</i>

08:28.891 --> 08:30.434
<i>separates Napoli from Firenze.</i>

08:30.934 --> 08:35.434
<i>At the midway point lies Roma,
one and a half hours away</i>

08:38.108 --> 08:40.360
Aw, now we're stuck…

08:40.402 --> 08:41.569
Shut up!

08:43.363 --> 08:45.865
Hey, there's a space
under this door.

08:45.908 --> 08:48.201
I wonder what's on the other side?

08:48.577 --> 08:51.204
Isn't that for the guy
who drives the train?

08:51.246 --> 08:55.746
No way those seven guys
are hiding in there.

08:57.836 --> 08:59.462
Can't tell for sure.

08:59.880 --> 09:02.757
Why don't you unleash Fisher Man
and find out?

09:07.679 --> 09:08.680
Do it.

09:10.933 --> 09:13.310
Fisher Man!

09:18.899 --> 09:23.111
I couldn't find seven guys
in there…

09:24.279 --> 09:25.613
But I did find two!

09:27.157 --> 09:28.158
Got 'em!

09:32.371 --> 09:34.790
Merda, it's a tight squeeze
for sure.

09:34.957 --> 09:36.708
Just room for the engineer.

09:36.875 --> 09:37.709
Well, it doesn't matter,

09:37.793 --> 09:40.128
'cause I know those bastards
are somewhere on this train.

09:40.379 --> 09:43.298
Huh? Hey, wait a second.

09:43.340 --> 09:45.091
I hooked only one of em?

09:45.300 --> 09:49.012
I could have sworn I detected
two hearts thumping away in there.

09:49.721 --> 09:51.973
There was something else in there…

09:52.015 --> 09:53.016
Hey, Pesci!

09:53.225 --> 09:54.768
Get your ass ready
'cause we're gonna

09:54.810 --> 09:56.603
search every centimeter
of the train!

09:56.645 --> 09:58.146
We'll find Bucciarati and his men,

09:58.188 --> 09:59.689
and we'll rip them out
from their hiding spot!

09:59.898 --> 10:01.316
And I want you to stay right here.

10:01.358 --> 10:02.108
Huh?

10:02.109 --> 10:04.694
If they figure out we're here,

10:04.778 --> 10:07.530
you can bet your butt they'll
come here to stop the train.

10:07.572 --> 10:09.031
I gotcha covered, big bro!

10:09.157 --> 10:11.534
Don't forget, they're traveling
with company.

10:11.618 --> 10:14.120
They can't just cut loose
down the aisles

10:14.162 --> 10:15.246
or jump off a speeding train

10:15.330 --> 10:17.165
when they feel like it.

10:17.207 --> 10:19.584
That's what gives us
the upper hand.

10:19.668 --> 10:21.044
By the time we make it
to Roma Termini,

10:21.086 --> 10:22.378
those bastards
are gonna be mortadella

10:22.421 --> 10:24.297
and the girl will be ours!

10:28.885 --> 10:30.678
The key wasn't made to fit
in a keyhole.

10:30.721 --> 10:34.808
It fit perfectly in the shell
of this turtle.

10:35.225 --> 10:38.811
Somehow, that activated
the turtle's special ability.

10:39.021 --> 10:42.232
The key functions as a portal
to an alternate space,

10:42.441 --> 10:44.734
a space where
we can remain sight unseen.

10:45.402 --> 10:47.987
Th-The turtle is a Stand user?

10:51.158 --> 10:52.492
<i>O-Ow!</i>

10:52.701 --> 10:53.827
<i>W-Where the hell am I?</i>

10:54.745 --> 10:56.371
<i>I'm under the seat?</i>

10:57.664 --> 10:58.665
Ow!

10:59.333 --> 11:02.044
B-But shit, this is so cool!

11:02.085 --> 11:04.295
This turtle is like
some kind of spaceship!

11:04.588 --> 11:08.258
But this room isn't
some kind of illusion.

11:09.051 --> 11:11.053
It's a bona fide structure.

11:11.094 --> 11:13.221
Look, this couch,
this furniture is real.

11:13.347 --> 11:15.223
Even the freakin' drinks are cold.

11:15.599 --> 11:18.935
I suppose the boss is responsible
for making these arrangements.

11:19.186 --> 11:21.438
For the most part,
turtles prefer dark spaces,

11:21.521 --> 11:24.273
and will most often
remain quiet and motionless.

11:24.316 --> 11:25.525
In other words,
we should be able to

11:25.567 --> 11:27.944
travel to Venezia
unnoticed and unharmed.

11:30.906 --> 11:34.159
Guess no one would be
hiding in here…

11:34.242 --> 11:37.370
My gut doesn't talk to me
like big bro's does.

11:48.131 --> 11:49.465
Big bro!

11:49.758 --> 11:51.301
Did he really…?

11:53.095 --> 11:55.597
Thankful Death!

11:57.057 --> 11:58.808
You're gonna do it?

11:58.850 --> 12:01.269
You're gonna do it to everyone?!

12:01.311 --> 12:04.856
We don't even know if
they're on this train!

12:04.940 --> 12:06.483
I already told you,

12:06.817 --> 12:08.652
not a centimeter of this train
is safe for them!

12:09.277 --> 12:11.487
Those bastards are here, I know it.

12:11.613 --> 12:14.115
Sides, you're making
a fuss over nothing.

12:14.157 --> 12:18.327
Planes fall from the sky
all the time, anyway.

12:18.745 --> 12:20.997
These guys are lucky
they got it so easy.

12:29.548 --> 12:31.550
MR. PRESIDENT
COCO LARGE

12:50.318 --> 12:52.987
Guess being stuck inside
a turtle has its drawbacks.

12:53.029 --> 12:54.530
It's kinda muggy.

12:55.157 --> 12:57.951
You want a drink, too, Narancia?

12:58.702 --> 13:00.578
Hope you like 'em cold
'cause that's all we got.

13:00.704 --> 13:04.999
There's cola, mineral water,
sparkling and still,

13:05.041 --> 13:07.334
apple, orange, and pineapple juice.

13:08.128 --> 13:09.671
Hey, you listening?

13:11.047 --> 13:13.507
Huh? What was that?!

13:13.550 --> 13:15.802
I'm asking if you want
something to drink!

13:16.178 --> 13:18.388
You might wanna try
to get some shut eye.

13:18.638 --> 13:20.348
You've seen better days there,
my man.

13:20.390 --> 13:22.558
I'll keep an eye
on the ceiling.

13:22.851 --> 13:24.435
Oh, okay!

13:24.936 --> 13:28.105
You know, my shoulders
are kinda hurting,

13:28.190 --> 13:31.902
and my back doesn't feel
great either. There we go…

13:32.194 --> 13:34.946
Something warm would really
hit the spot…

13:35.447 --> 13:36.906
Something gentle on my gut.

13:37.073 --> 13:40.284
For the last time,
all we got are cold ones!

13:40.368 --> 13:42.995
Your brain shuts down
when people talk to you, huh?!

13:43.413 --> 13:45.581
Banana it is then.

13:48.793 --> 13:51.545
Gardens like these really
sooth the soul, don't they?

13:51.713 --> 13:53.589
Stress melts away…

13:54.549 --> 13:56.551
So heavenly…

13:57.010 --> 14:00.096
Oh, how I'd love to bask in that
Garden of Eden's warm sunshine,

14:00.180 --> 14:03.808
just daydreaming about
the good old days.

14:07.479 --> 14:09.481
Hey, cut that shit out!

14:09.564 --> 14:12.900
Nobody wants your gross ass spit
on the pages! Christ!

14:13.235 --> 14:15.946
Huh? I did what?

14:16.112 --> 14:18.614
Me? No way!

14:27.415 --> 14:30.084
Hey, you're drooling
pretty bad there, man.

14:30.126 --> 14:32.837
That is so freakin' nasty.
What the heck is that?

14:32.921 --> 14:33.922
Hey!

14:37.133 --> 14:38.134
A tooth?

14:38.885 --> 14:43.385
There's no way I can
eat this banana…

14:44.599 --> 14:47.143
It's like a piece of old,
stale beef jerky…

14:47.269 --> 14:51.648
Hey… You really got me good there.

14:52.732 --> 14:54.316
Scared me for a second…

14:54.401 --> 14:57.654
That thing really
looks like a tooth.

14:57.737 --> 15:01.824
That was totally disgusting,
and a little too far if you ask me…

15:01.908 --> 15:04.160
What is that hanging
from your mouth?

15:04.452 --> 15:08.952
Huh? Did you say
something again, Mista?

15:09.958 --> 15:13.503
Gotta speak up… Can't hear ya…

15:13.587 --> 15:16.673
These ears don't seem to be working
very well right now…

15:17.299 --> 15:21.761
This darn banana is
falling apart, you know?

15:22.470 --> 15:25.181
I-I can't eat it…

15:26.016 --> 15:29.978
Th-They're all old and rotten…

15:30.145 --> 15:33.189
This fruit has gone bad…

15:33.231 --> 15:34.857
W-What the hell is with you?!

15:34.941 --> 15:36.859
- You look like you've had
- Didn't you hear me?

15:36.901 --> 15:38.903
- One helluva rough night!
- Okay, then…

15:38.987 --> 15:41.030
- N-Narancia, you…
- I'll say it in a voice

15:41.072 --> 15:42.198
you can hear this time!

15:42.240 --> 15:44.158
This better?!

15:44.534 --> 15:47.995
There's no way in God's name
I can eat this damn banana!

15:48.038 --> 15:52.042
Look, it's falling apart
as I hold it…

15:52.250 --> 15:54.335
It's way past its prime…

15:54.377 --> 15:55.169
Bucciarati!

15:55.211 --> 15:57.421
There's no question…
This is a Stand!

15:57.756 --> 16:00.967
One of them made it
on board this train!

16:01.509 --> 16:05.095
Huh? What?
What's with all this gray stuff?

16:05.180 --> 16:08.308
This tuft of hair slipped
right out of my very own scalp…

16:08.350 --> 16:11.061
What the hell is this?!

16:11.770 --> 16:13.229
What's the matter?

16:13.772 --> 16:16.733
Did something… happen?

16:19.944 --> 16:21.695
Th-They're all geriatrics!

16:26.242 --> 16:30.246
Mama… Wake up… Wake up…

16:30.664 --> 16:33.291
Mama… Mama…

16:35.543 --> 16:38.546
Wake up…

16:41.883 --> 16:46.383
Wh-Who the hell is that?

16:46.721 --> 16:50.182
What? No way… This can't be!

16:50.225 --> 16:52.602
This is me?!

16:53.061 --> 16:55.521
What the hell's going on?

16:56.189 --> 16:58.316
A-An age accelerating Stand?

16:58.400 --> 16:59.901
Did they figure us out?

17:00.110 --> 17:02.487
Do they know we're hiding
in this turtle?!

17:02.570 --> 17:03.821
Keep your cool, Mista.

17:03.988 --> 17:06.699
If they knew about
our reptilian bunker,

17:06.950 --> 17:09.285
they would have launched a swifter,
more direct attack.

17:10.453 --> 17:14.123
They're trying to root us out
because they can't find us.

17:14.541 --> 17:16.626
You can bet the one thing
they do know

17:16.668 --> 17:19.379
is that we're somewhere
on this train.

17:19.629 --> 17:21.631
To track down the boss's daughter,

17:21.715 --> 17:23.049
they're going to take down

17:23.091 --> 17:24.467
every man, woman, and child
on this train!

17:25.760 --> 17:28.387
You mean to tell me this train is
careening down the tracks

17:28.430 --> 17:30.807
chock full of seniors
on death's door?

17:31.433 --> 17:32.642
In a word.

17:32.767 --> 17:35.853
They're desperate.
They'll do anything necessary.

17:35.937 --> 17:37.730
They won't even bat an eye.

17:38.148 --> 17:40.400
What all this means, ragazzo,
is that we have two choices.

17:40.775 --> 17:43.652
We take Trish and get
the hell off this train.

17:44.154 --> 17:47.532
Or we ignore the fact that
we don't know our attacker's range

17:47.615 --> 17:49.325
and we hunt them down anyway.

17:49.409 --> 17:50.993
Well, duh, number two.

17:51.161 --> 17:52.829
If we want to escape with Trish,

17:52.912 --> 17:54.663
we'll have to stop this thing
dead in its tracks.

17:55.081 --> 17:56.499
Jumping while moving is
a death wish.

17:58.001 --> 18:00.336
Assassination is
our ace in the hole…

18:00.462 --> 18:03.715
With my Six Bullets, that is!

18:03.798 --> 18:06.175
Esatto… You're precisely right.

18:06.342 --> 18:08.052
But we're completely out of time.

18:08.303 --> 18:10.805
Our bodies are aging
at blinding speed…

18:11.139 --> 18:13.266
B-Bucciarati…

18:13.558 --> 18:15.184
M-My hands…

18:18.605 --> 18:22.150
My skin and nails are
just falling off!

18:23.151 --> 18:25.194
They're disintegrating!

18:26.070 --> 18:29.698
You're right, Bucciarati.
We're shit out of time!

18:30.992 --> 18:33.077
Wait a minute, Mista…

18:33.745 --> 18:36.497
It's too early… to go…

18:36.539 --> 18:39.041
What the hell kind of crazy
are you speaking now, Giorno?

18:39.125 --> 18:42.378
I'm telling you.
It's too early to go…

18:42.879 --> 18:44.589
We can't waste another second!

18:44.672 --> 18:45.422
Wait.

18:45.465 --> 18:46.466
Just listen.

18:46.841 --> 18:49.093
What are you trying
to say, Giorno?

18:49.344 --> 18:53.844
Why do you think we're aging
at different rates from Bucciarati?

18:57.310 --> 18:59.937
The aging effects have hit Mista
and me a lot less…

19:00.021 --> 19:01.647
Trish's better off than us!

19:01.856 --> 19:03.065
But why?

19:03.149 --> 19:05.609
So we lucked out and got better
genes than everyone else…

19:05.693 --> 19:06.652
I'm outta here!

19:06.694 --> 19:08.904
No… If they're blindly attacking

19:08.988 --> 19:11.699
everything that moves
on this train…

19:12.158 --> 19:14.493
then they must know
they could also very easily

19:14.536 --> 19:16.371
end up killing the girl too.

19:17.330 --> 19:20.041
The speed of the aging
has to be conditional.

19:20.667 --> 19:22.418
I'll cut right to the chase.

19:23.044 --> 19:25.337
I think our enemy can
discern man from woman

19:25.421 --> 19:28.757
by identifying differences
in body temperature.

19:29.551 --> 19:32.262
I once read somewhere that because

19:32.345 --> 19:35.765
women have a greater body fat
percentage than men,

19:35.807 --> 19:38.226
their body temperature
tends to be more stable.

19:38.268 --> 19:41.187
Women's cells also tend to
age slower than men's,

19:41.229 --> 19:43.648
which is why they supposedly
live longer.

19:43.982 --> 19:46.943
Don't you think it's been
a little hot?

19:46.985 --> 19:50.279
They're controlling
the speed of aging

19:50.405 --> 19:52.949
by observing the subtle changes
of our body temperatures.

19:53.157 --> 19:54.366
It's simple.

19:54.617 --> 19:56.744
All you have to keep in mind is
that men age faster than women.

19:56.786 --> 19:59.455
Well, yeah, when you put it
that way, it all sounds great.

19:59.539 --> 20:01.123
But then, how do you explain why

20:01.207 --> 20:02.625
I'm doing just fine
and you're an old fogey?

20:02.709 --> 20:04.293
You saying I'm some kind
of chick or something?!

20:04.377 --> 20:05.628
Body temperature…

20:07.005 --> 20:08.798
Actually, our body temperatures

20:08.882 --> 20:11.009
would be slightly cooler
than theirs…

20:11.134 --> 20:13.386
We both were sipping down
cold drinks.

20:13.595 --> 20:15.471
Narancia didn't have
anything to drink.

20:21.185 --> 20:22.227
Th-That's…

20:22.770 --> 20:25.189
Giorno, holy shit,
you were exactly right!

20:25.273 --> 20:29.068
We're aging at a slower rate
because our bodies were cooler!

20:30.028 --> 20:33.406
Time to start cooling…
Get some ice and cool 'em down!

20:33.531 --> 20:34.865
Hold it, Mista!

20:34.949 --> 20:37.326
You're going to have to figure out
a way to take that ice with you!

20:39.078 --> 20:40.829
Th-This is all we got?

20:41.080 --> 20:42.122
In case you forgot,

20:42.165 --> 20:44.167
everything still depends on
destroying this enemy.

20:44.250 --> 20:46.043
Mista, the ice will be imperative

20:46.127 --> 20:48.379
in being able to
defeat this killer…

20:48.630 --> 20:49.881
You have to do the deed

20:49.964 --> 20:52.925
before your Stand and
the ice disappears completely.

20:57.972 --> 21:02.017
Just the driver…
Looks like everyone else is gone.

21:07.148 --> 21:08.566
It's hot as hell…

21:08.858 --> 21:12.987
This bastard really is
attacking everything in sight.

21:13.821 --> 21:16.281
I wonder if our little slowpoke
is aging too.

21:16.324 --> 21:19.076
Don't they live for like
a bazillion years or something?

21:19.327 --> 21:21.245
Guess he'll outlive us.

21:21.746 --> 21:23.289
Damn it…

21:23.373 --> 21:27.293
Big bro,
you're gonna get me killed.

21:33.508 --> 21:38.008
What's gonna happen if
I start gettin' old, porca put tan a?

21:38.179 --> 21:39.263
The air conditioner?

21:39.639 --> 21:41.307
If I can turn on
the air in the car,

21:41.349 --> 21:43.309
that should cool down
the turtle and everyone in there,

21:43.351 --> 21:46.103
and then, I might be able to
slow down that freaky aging!

21:48.523 --> 21:49.565
Presto!

21:49.607 --> 21:51.984
I got a feisty one!

21:54.362 --> 21:57.281
<i>What the hell is this frickin' hook
doing under my skin?!</i>

21:57.824 --> 22:00.993
<i>This isn't the guy trying
to age us to death?</i>

22:01.160 --> 22:04.037
<i>There's another one?
There are two of them?</i>

22:04.372 --> 22:06.123
<i>Two freaks want us dead now?!</i>

23:38.299 --> 23:42.094
EPISODE 15
THANKFUL DEATH, PART 1
